00:15:58.080 --> 00:15:58.920
Exactly.

579
00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:00.080
The symptom is avoidance.

580
00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:02.560
The cure is exposure.

581
00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:03.920
If the ultimate fix

582
00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:04.880
for the engine of fear

583
00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:06.200
across all these conditions

584
00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:07.840
is to actively face it,

585
00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:09.040
to intentionally recreate

586
00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:10.080
the panic attack,

587
00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:11.120
or to intentionally walk

588
00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:12.920
into the crowded room,

589
00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:13.760
what does that tell us

590
00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:14.920
about the fundamental nature

591
00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:16.080
of fear itself?

592
00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:17.400
It suggests something profound

593
00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:18.840
about the human condition.

594
00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:20.120
It suggests that fear actually

595
00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:21.400
runs on the very avoidance

596
00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:22.560
we use to try and protect

597
00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:23.320
ourselves from it.

598
00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:23.960
Wow.

599
00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:25.800
So every time we step away,

600
00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:26.880
we are feeding it.

601
00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:27.920
Precisely.

602
00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:28.720
Every time we choose

603
00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:29.720
the quick fix sedative,

604
00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:30.920
or skip the concert,

605
00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:31.880
or avoid the difficult

606
00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.080
conversation,

607
00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:34.320
we think we are putting

608
00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:35.400
the fire out.

609
00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:36.200
Because we feel

610
00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:37.520
that immediate relief.

611
00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:38.120
Right.

612
00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:39.880
But mechanically, we are pouring

613
00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:41.560
fuel directly into the fear

614
00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:42.360
engine.

615
00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:44.000
We are confirming to the brain's

616
00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:45.520
threat detection center

617
00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:47.200
that the situation was indeed

618
00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:48.240
life threatening,

619
00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:49.480
and that running away was

620
00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:51.480
the only reason we survived.

621
00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:52.640
So we are basically

622
00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:54.680
cementing the neuroplastic

623
00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.080
pathway of fear.

624
00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:57.080
We feed the engine

625
00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:58.080
by running away.

626
00:16:58.080 --> 00:16:59.280
Which means the only way

627
00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:00.280
to starve the engine

628
00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:01.840
is to stand still,

629
00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:03.120
to let the exhaust wash

630
00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.480
over you until your amygdala

631
00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:05.920
finally realizes it's just

632
00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:06.480
smoke.

633
00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:06.960
Yes.

634
00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:07.800
It completely flips

635
00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:08.720
our survival instincts

636
00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:09.440
upside down.

637
00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:10.520
You have to move toward

638
00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:11.320
the thing your brain is

639
00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:12.560
screaming at you to run from.

640
00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:14.040
It is the ultimate paradox

641
00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:15.040
of anxiety.

642
00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:16.200
Healing requires you

643
00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:17.600
to tolerate the discomfort

644
00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:18.400
you have spent your whole

645
00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:19.680
life trying to escape.

646
00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:21.840
And that is a really powerful

647
00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.200
realization to walk away

648
00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.640
with today.

649
00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.000
Thank you so much for joining us

650
00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:27.080
on this deep dive.

651
00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:27.840
We hope this look

652
00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:28.600
at the engine of fear

653
00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:30.000
gives you a new lens to view

654
00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.600
not just clinical diagnoses,

655
00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:32.960
but the everyday anxieties

656
00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:33.920
we all navigate.

657
00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:34.720
Absolutely.

658
00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:35.520
The next time you feel

659
00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:36.760
the engine revving,

660
00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:39.040
don't run from the exhaust.

661
00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:39.920
Keep questioning,

662
00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:41.360
keep exploring,

663
00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:42.440
and remember to look closely

664
00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:43.480
at the shape of the things

665
00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:44.240
that scare you.

666
00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:45.120
We'll catch you next time.
